{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-blog-index-feature-banner
  Full-bleed editorial banner that sits below the editorial section on
  /blogs/field-notes. Maude pattern: side-to-side photo with a white
  text overlay (topic + title + excerpt + optional link).

  Audience-aware: each block carries an audience tag (all/kids/adults).
  Only the block matching the current audience shows. The audience
  itself comes from the editorial section's toggle via:
    - localStorage key 'field-notes-audience' (read on init)
    - 'field-notes:audience-changed' window event (live updates)
  Falls back to the 'all' block when no exact match exists.

  Mobile: same overlay treatment, slightly less padding so the title
  doesn't clip on narrow viewports.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign min_height = section.settings.min_height_desktop | default: 80
  assign min_height_mobile = section.settings.min_height_mobile | default: 70

  comment
    Auto-pull (added 2026-05-26): when a banner block has no Article
    picked, fall back to the freshest matching article from the blog
    based on the block's audience setting. Lets banner-kids and
    banner-adults auto-populate without manual curation; banner-all
    can still curate by setting an Article in admin.

    Priority per audience:
      kids   : first kids article → first mixed/blank → first adults
      adults : first adults article → first mixed/blank → first kids
      all    : freshest blog article regardless of audience
  endcomment
  comment
    Skip the FIRST kids and FIRST adults article: the editorial
    section above already auto-pulls those as its per-audience feature
    cards, and we want the banner to surface a different article
    rather than duplicating the page hero. The 2nd-in-bucket article
    is what each audience banner shows. Falls through to mixed/newest
    when fewer than two matching articles exist.
  endcomment
  assign kids_handle_auto = ''
  assign adults_handle_auto = ''
  assign mixed_handle_auto = ''
  assign newest_handle_auto = ''
  assign kids_seen = 0
  assign adults_seen = 0
  for a in blog.articles limit: 50
    if newest_handle_auto == ''
      assign newest_handle_auto = a.handle
    endif
    assign ra = a.metafields.field_notes.read_audience | downcase
    if ra == 'kids'
      assign kids_seen = kids_seen | plus: 1
      if kids_seen > 1 and kids_handle_auto == ''
        assign kids_handle_auto = a.handle
      endif
    elsif ra == 'parents' or ra == 'adults'
      assign adults_seen = adults_seen | plus: 1
      if adults_seen > 1 and adults_handle_auto == ''
        assign adults_handle_auto = a.handle
      endif
    elsif mixed_handle_auto == ''
      assign mixed_handle_auto = a.handle
    endif
  endfor
-%}

<section
  class="theinmag-feature-banner"
  data-theinmag-feature-banner
  style="--banner-min-h-desktop: {{ min_height }}vh; --banner-min-h-mobile: {{ min_height_mobile }}vh;"
>
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign article = block.settings.article

      comment
        Auto-pull fallback: when no Article is picked, resolve a recent
        matching article from blog.articles by the block's audience
        setting so the banner stays content-fresh without admin curation.
      endcomment
      if article == blank
        assign block_aud = block.settings.audience | default: 'all'
        assign auto_handle = ''
        if block_aud == 'kids'
          assign auto_handle = kids_handle_auto
          if auto_handle == ''
            assign auto_handle = mixed_handle_auto
          endif
          if auto_handle == ''
            assign auto_handle = newest_handle_auto
          endif
        elsif block_aud == 'adults'
          assign auto_handle = adults_handle_auto
          if auto_handle == ''
            assign auto_handle = mixed_handle_auto
          endif
          if auto_handle == ''
            assign auto_handle = newest_handle_auto
          endif
        else
          assign auto_handle = newest_handle_auto
        endif
        if auto_handle != ''
          assign auto_resolved = articles[auto_handle]
          if auto_resolved != blank
            assign article = auto_resolved
          endif
        endif
      endif

      comment
        Priority flip 2026-05-18: when Article (picked or auto-pulled) is
        set, article data wins. Overrides only apply when no Article is
        available at all (true placeholder fallback before any post
        exists). Matches the editorial card snippet behaviour.
      endcomment
      if article != blank
        assign title = article.title

        assign excerpt = article.excerpt | strip_html
        if excerpt == blank
          assign excerpt = article.content | strip_html | truncatewords: 24
        endif

        assign topic = article.metafields.field_notes.primary_topic
        if topic == blank
          assign topic = article.tags.first
        endif

        assign banner_link = article.url

        assign image_src = ''
        if article.image != blank
          assign image_src = article.image | image_url: width: 2400
        endif

        assign image_alt = article.image.alt | default: article.title

        comment
          Routing audience comes from the block setting, not the
          article's metafield. The block setting is intent (this
          banner is for kids/adults/all); the article metafield is
          content classification. A mixed article rendered in the
          adults banner block is fine - it shows when the visitor
          flips to adults because the BLOCK is tagged adults.
        endcomment
        assign audience = block.settings.audience | default: 'all'

        assign cta_label = block.settings.cta_label
      else
        assign title = block.settings.title_override
        assign excerpt = block.settings.excerpt_override
        assign topic = block.settings.topic
        assign banner_link = block.settings.link_override

        assign image_src = ''
        if block.settings.image != blank
          assign image_src = block.settings.image | image_url: width: 2400
        elsif block.settings.fallback_filename != blank
          assign image_src = block.settings.fallback_filename | asset_url
        endif

        assign image_alt = block.settings.image_alt | default: title
        assign audience = block.settings.audience | default: 'all'
        assign cta_label = block.settings.cta_label
      endif

      comment
        Real Kids Voices covers (kid artwork) anchor to the top so the
        subject's head isn't cropped by the banner's cover fill.
      endcomment
      assign is_kid_art = false
      if article != blank and article.metafields.field_notes.kid_first_name != blank
        assign is_kid_art = true
      endif
    -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Whole panel is the click target - cleaner than a tucked-away CTA
      button inside the copy block. When a link exists we wrap in <a>;
      otherwise the panel renders as a plain <article>.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture banner_inner -%}
      {%- if image_src != blank -%}
        <img
          class="theinmag-feature-banner__image{% if is_kid_art %} theinmag-feature-banner__image--top{% endif %}"
          src="{{ image_src }}"
          alt="{{ image_alt | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
          width="2400"
          height="1350"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="theinmag-feature-banner__placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <span class="theinmag-feature-banner__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="theinmag-feature-banner__copy">
        {%- if topic != blank -%}
          <span class="theinmag-feature-banner__topic">{{ topic }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if title != blank -%}
          <h2 class="theinmag-feature-banner__title">{{ title }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if excerpt != blank -%}
          <p class="theinmag-feature-banner__excerpt">{{ excerpt }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- if banner_link != blank -%}
      <a
        class="theinmag-feature-banner__panel theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link"
        href="{{ banner_link }}"
        data-banner-panel
        data-audience="{{ audience }}"
        hidden
        {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
      >{{ banner_inner }}</a>
    {%- else -%}
      <article
        class="theinmag-feature-banner__panel"
        data-banner-panel
        data-audience="{{ audience }}"
        hidden
        {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
      >{{ banner_inner }}</article>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</section>

{%- stylesheet -%}
  /* ================================================================
     Full-bleed banner - breaks out of the lavender section's max
     width to span the full viewport. Negative margins handle the
     break-out without needing to restructure the parent template.
     ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-feature-banner {
    position: relative;
    width: 100vw;
    margin-left: calc(50% - 50vw);
    margin-right: calc(50% - 50vw);
    background-color: #2A1F3D;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: var(--banner-min-h-mobile, 70vh);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: opacity 0.32s ease, transform 0.32s ease;
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-feature-banner__panel {
      min-height: var(--banner-min-h-desktop, 80vh);
    }
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner.is-leaving .theinmag-feature-banner__panel {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateX(-16px);
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__image {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  /* Kid-art covers (Real Kids Voices) anchor to the top so the subject's
     head stays in frame rather than being cropped by the cover fill. */
  .theinmag-feature-banner__image--top {
    object-position: top center;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__placeholder {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #5D3A7A 0%, #C9543E 100%);
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to top,
      rgba(20, 14, 30, 0.78) 0%,
      rgba(20, 14, 30, 0.42) 35%,
      rgba(20, 14, 30, 0.10) 60%,
      rgba(20, 14, 30, 0) 80%
    );
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__copy {
    position: absolute;
    left: clamp(20px, 5vw, 80px);
    right: clamp(20px, 5vw, 80px);
    bottom: clamp(40px, 6vw, 88px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    color: #FFFFFF;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* Type sizes match the editorial feature card's on-photo treatment
     so the two photo-overlay surfaces on the page read as siblings
     rather than the banner shouting over the editorial header. */
  .theinmag-feature-banner__topic {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4.8vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45), 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    padding-bottom: 0.08em;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__excerpt {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    opacity: 0.95;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  /* Whole-panel link variant - subtle hover lift on the image so the
     visitor feels the click target without needing a CTA button. */
  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link .theinmag-feature-banner__image {
    transition: transform 0.5s ease;
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link:hover .theinmag-feature-banner__image,
  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link:focus-visible .theinmag-feature-banner__image {
    transform: scale(1.02);
  }

  .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #FFFFFF;
    outline-offset: -6px;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-feature-banner__panel,
    .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link .theinmag-feature-banner__image {
      transition: none;
    }
    .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link:hover .theinmag-feature-banner__image,
    .theinmag-feature-banner__panel--link:focus-visible .theinmag-feature-banner__image {
      transform: none;
    }
    .theinmag-feature-banner.is-leaving .theinmag-feature-banner__panel {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
{%- endstylesheet -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    var section = document.querySelector('[data-theinmag-feature-banner]');
    if (!section) return;

    var STORAGE_KEY = 'field-notes-audience';
    var EVENT_NAME = 'field-notes:audience-changed';
    var TRANSITION_MS = 320;
    var reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    var panels = Array.prototype.slice.call(section.querySelectorAll('[data-banner-panel]'));
    if (!panels.length) return;

    function audienceKey(p) { return p.dataset.audience || 'all'; }

    function pickPanel(audience) {
      // Prefer exact match. Fall back to 'all'. Fall back to first panel.
      var exact = panels.find(function (p) { return audienceKey(p) === audience; });
      if (exact) return exact;
      var any = panels.find(function (p) { return audienceKey(p) === 'all'; });
      if (any) return any;
      return panels[0];
    }

    function showOnly(panel) {
      panels.forEach(function (p) {
        p.hidden = (p !== panel);
      });
    }

    /* ---------- Hero/banner collision guard ----------------------
       The banner picks its article either from admin curation or
       from the auto-pull skip-first logic (Liquid above). Both
       defenses can fail in edge cases - someone curates the same
       article in both spots, or the blog runs short on audience-
       matched articles so the editorial fallback and the banner
       fallback land on the same handle. This runtime check looks at
       the visible editorial pool's feature card href and, if the
       active banner panel matches, hides the banner so the same
       article never displays twice on the same page.
       --------------------------------------------------------- */
    function visibleEditorialFeatureHref() {
      var pool = document.querySelector('.theinmag-editorial [data-audience-pool]:not([hidden])');
      if (!pool) return '';
      var feat = pool.querySelector('.theinmag-editorial__card--feature');
      return feat ? (feat.getAttribute('href') || '') : '';
    }

    function applyCollisionGuard() {
      var editorialHref = visibleEditorialFeatureHref();
      if (!editorialHref) return;
      panels.forEach(function (p) {
        if (p.hidden) return; // only consider the panel currently meant to be visible
        var panelHref = p.getAttribute('href');
        if (panelHref && panelHref === editorialHref) {
          p.hidden = true;
        }
      });
    }

    function applyAudience(audience, animate) {
      var target = pickPanel(audience);
      if (!target) return;

      if (animate && !reduced) {
        section.classList.add('is-leaving');
        setTimeout(function () {
          showOnly(target);
          applyCollisionGuard();
          window.requestAnimationFrame(function () {
            section.classList.remove('is-leaving');
          });
        }, TRANSITION_MS);
      } else {
        showOnly(target);
        applyCollisionGuard();
      }
    }

    /* Init from localStorage so the banner matches whatever the visitor
       last selected, even on a fresh page load. */
    var initial = 'all';
    try { initial = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) || 'all'; } catch (e) {}
    if (initial !== 'all' && initial !== 'kids' && initial !== 'adults') initial = 'all';
    applyAudience(initial, false);

    window.addEventListener(EVENT_NAME, function (e) {
      if (!e || !e.detail) return;
      applyAudience(e.detail.audience, !!e.detail.animate);
    });
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "field notes banner",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "theinmag-feature-banner-section",
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Banner sizing"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height_desktop",
      "label": "Desktop min height",
      "min": 50,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "vh",
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height_mobile",
      "label": "Mobile min height",
      "min": 50,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "vh",
      "default": 70
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Add up to three banner blocks - one per audience (all / kids / adults). The block matching the visitor's current toggle is shown; the others stay hidden in the DOM ready to swap in. The 'all' block is the fallback when no exact match exists."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "audience_banner",
      "name": "Audience banner",
      "limit": 3,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "audience",
          "label": "Audience",
          "options": [
            { "value": "all", "label": "All" },
            { "value": "kids", "label": "Kids" },
            { "value": "adults", "label": "Adults" }
          ],
          "default": "all"
        },
        { "type": "article", "id": "article", "label": "Article" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "topic", "label": "Topic label" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title_override", "label": "Title override" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "excerpt_override", "label": "Excerpt override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "link_override", "label": "Link override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "CTA label", "info": "Defaults to 'read this one' if blank." },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Banner image" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "fallback_filename", "label": "Banner image fallback filename" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Banner image alt text" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "field notes banner",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "audience_banner",
          "settings": {
            "audience": "all",
            "topic": "Behind the mag",
            "title_override": "what mag10 looks like in the wild.",
            "excerpt_override": "From the kitchen table to the school library, here's where this issue is landing.",
            "fallback_filename": "blog-image-universal-12.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Mag10 in the wild - placeholder banner.",
            "link_override": "/blogs/field-notes",
            "cta_label": "Read this one"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "audience_banner",
          "settings": {
            "audience": "kids",
            "topic": "Make your own",
            "title_override": "the fold-and-snip zine, in 60 seconds.",
            "excerpt_override": "One sheet of paper. One scissor. One tiny eight-page magazine of your own.",
            "fallback_filename": "blog-image-universal-13.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Fold-and-snip zine - placeholder banner.",
            "link_override": "/blogs/field-notes",
            "cta_label": "Show me how"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "audience_banner",
          "settings": {
            "audience": "adults",
            "topic": "Read aloud",
            "title_override": "what changes when you read aloud at night.",
            "excerpt_override": "More than vocabulary. More than bonding. The quiet rewiring no one mentions.",
            "fallback_filename": "blog-image-universal-14.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Read aloud at night - placeholder banner.",
            "link_override": "/blogs/field-notes",
            "cta_label": "Read this one"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
